# Engineering rules

- Keep dataset, audio, ASR, NLU, risk analysis, controller, evaluation and UI as separate modules.
- Use typed dataclasses or validated schemas for sample and prediction objects.
- Avoid hidden global state and implicit file paths.
- Use explicit configuration.
- Keep core pipeline usable without Streamlit.
- Keep local inference as the default.
- Isolate external service adapters behind interfaces.
- Handle empty audio, missing files, malformed model outputs, timeout and exceptions explicitly.
- Never silently convert a failed stage into a successful prediction.
- Emit structured per-stage traces with sample ID, run ID, stage, duration, status and reason.
- Add tests for normal, boundary and failure cases.
- Avoid broad exception swallowing.
- If an exception is handled, preserve diagnostic context.
- Do not add dependencies without explaining why they are needed.
